 \section*{Data and code}
 
-Every number in this paper can be reproduced from the repository at \url{https://github.com/BrettRey/prediction-checker}, which holds a script that downloads every public source used, the frozen prediction record, the scripts that read the report's figures and check them against its text, the design analysis, and the outcome analysis, with the CRTC series used (Open Government Licence~-- Canada). The analysis plan and each choice made after the outcome data was opened are recorded with dates in the repository. The case was first suggested in a list of candidate cases produced by ChatGPT (the latest model available on 3 October 2026, at the Pro effort level), which also proposed separating the report's technical claim from the public argument. It supplied leads and reported forecast figures, every one of which was checked against primary sources before use, and none of the calculations reported here. The analysis scripts were written with Claude Opus 5.5; independent checks of the numbers, the inference, the quotations and the fairness of the account were run with GPT-6 Astra (through Codex), and their findings were verified against the sources before any change was made.
